WEBVTT

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:37.329
Your call is being...

00:00:37.412 --> 00:00:38.997
...connected...

00:00:39.081 --> 00:00:40.290
...by SewerCom.

00:00:40.374 --> 00:00:42.251
Reach out and touch the sewers.

00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:45.629
Look, Morris, it's Leela calling.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.464
Hi, Mom, hi, Dad.

00:00:47.548 --> 00:00:49.383
Ready for your big trip to the surface?

00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:50.759
We're excited, honey,

00:00:50.843 --> 00:00:52.803
but we don't want to embarrass you.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.138
I mean, your mother and I
are basically monsters.

00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:56.515
Dad, relax.

00:00:56.598 --> 00:00:58.600
You are being so mutant.

00:00:58.684 --> 00:01:02.271
I found this adorable little bag
to wear over my head.

00:01:02.354 --> 00:01:03.772
And it was on sale.

00:01:03.856 --> 00:01:06.441
No one's wearing anything
adorable over their head.

00:01:06.525 --> 00:01:07.568
Now, listen.

00:01:07.651 --> 00:01:10.362
I could never ever
be ashamed of my parents.

00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:11.864
I'll see you this weekend.

00:01:13.115 --> 00:01:15.742
Hey, guess who
I just got off the videophone with.

00:01:15.826 --> 00:01:16.827
No.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:17.953
My parents!

00:01:18.036 --> 00:01:20.330
They're coming up
from the sewers for a visit Sunday.

00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:22.875
Are you off your rocket?

00:01:22.958 --> 00:01:24.334
Your parents are mutants.

00:01:24.418 --> 00:01:26.378
It's illegal for them to come above ground

00:01:26.461 --> 00:01:28.422
'cause they're inferior genetic scum.

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:30.591
Uh, present company excluded, of course.

00:01:30.674 --> 00:01:34.011
I'm getting them a special one-day
surface permit from CitiHall.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:37.014
Ooh, while you're there,
could you pick me up a license to kill?

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:38.724
Sure. Bare hands or weapon?

00:01:38.807 --> 00:01:41.268
Uh, what does piano wire count as?

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.645
Good news, anyone.

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:48.275
The Swedish robot from Pi-kea
is here with the supercollider I ordered.

00:01:48.358 --> 00:01:50.777
Enjoy your affordable Swedish crap.

00:01:57.993 --> 00:01:59.828
Let's see what tools we'll need.

00:02:00.871 --> 00:02:02.164
Uh-huh.

00:02:02.247 --> 00:02:03.582
Uh-huh.

00:02:03.665 --> 00:02:04.833
Uh-huh.

00:02:04.917 --> 00:02:06.376
All right, we're all set.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:10.714
Nothing like the rustic wholesomeness
of working with one's own hands.

00:02:21.725 --> 00:02:23.769
Ah, there. Finished.

00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:25.479
And only six missing pieces.

00:02:25.562 --> 00:02:28.482
Those Swedes sure know
how to put in almost everything you need.

00:02:28.565 --> 00:02:31.068
Man, I'm sore all over.

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:34.112
I feel like I just went
10 rounds with mighty Thor.

00:02:34.196 --> 00:02:36.281
I feel like I was mauled by Jesus.

00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:39.868
I've got just the thing.

00:02:39.952 --> 00:02:43.330
Genuine miracle cream I bought
from a traveling salesman.

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:46.667
"Come one, come all," he said.

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:48.043
"Step right up."

00:02:48.126 --> 00:02:50.587
"This sounds too good
to be true," I thought.

00:02:50.671 --> 00:02:54.049
He said I looked like a smart young man.

00:02:54.132 --> 00:02:56.635
"So, is it a deal?" I inquired.

00:02:56.718 --> 00:03:00.138
Two hours later, he was gone
with 60 of my dollars.

00:03:00.264 --> 00:03:02.850
But I had the miracle cream.

00:03:05.269 --> 00:03:06.854
Bad news, nobody.

00:03:06.937 --> 00:03:09.231
The supercollider super exploded.

00:03:09.314 --> 00:03:13.193
I need you to take it back
and exchange it for a wobbly CD rack

00:03:13.277 --> 00:03:16.655
and some of those rancid meatballs.

00:03:20.158 --> 00:03:21.952
Excuse me. Hi. Do you have a minute?

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:23.912
I live in Jersey City
and my car broke down

00:03:23.996 --> 00:03:25.581
and I need to get back
'cause my aunt's real sick

00:03:25.664 --> 00:03:27.666
and she needs this medicine,
but I need money for the bus.

00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:29.751
So I'm mugging you.
Hand over your wallets.

00:03:29.835 --> 00:03:32.129
I don't believe that story for a second.

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:33.505
It doesn't matter, I'm mugging you.

00:03:33.589 --> 00:03:35.924
There's no bus to Jersey City.

00:03:36.091 --> 00:03:38.635
Give me your wallets now
or my robot will shoot.

00:03:38.719 --> 00:03:40.220
Don't make me hurt you.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:44.183
I'm too scared to find my pocket.

00:03:44.266 --> 00:03:47.269
Here, I'll just take off my pants
and give you those.

00:03:47.853 --> 00:03:49.980
Hey, I don't like what I'm seeing.

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.231
Give it to 'em, Andrew!

00:03:55.986 --> 00:03:57.487
Give it to 'em again, Andrew!

00:03:59.031 --> 00:04:00.157
Ah!

00:04:03.493 --> 00:04:04.494
What the...

00:04:04.578 --> 00:04:06.455
Laser-proof shirts, huh?

00:04:06.538 --> 00:04:07.623
I'll show you.

00:04:08.415 --> 00:04:10.709
Huh? Hey. Quit it.

00:04:11.752 --> 00:04:12.961
Hi-ya!

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:19.384
Foiled.

00:04:19.468 --> 00:04:20.802
And after years of planning.

00:04:20.886 --> 00:04:22.387
You're out of the gang.

00:04:24.473 --> 00:04:26.600
How did we manage to survive?

00:04:26.683 --> 00:04:28.894
What gave us those strange powers?

00:04:28.977 --> 00:04:31.688
Maybe we're all wearing magic rings
but they're invisible rings

00:04:31.772 --> 00:04:32.940
so we don't even realize it.

00:04:33.023 --> 00:04:34.441
Also, you can't feel the rings.

00:04:36.485 --> 00:04:37.528
Oh, Fry!

00:04:37.611 --> 00:04:39.279
Shut up and look at this.

00:04:39.947 --> 00:04:42.783
"May cause superpowers in humans."

00:04:42.866 --> 00:04:44.117
Wow.

00:04:44.201 --> 00:04:46.787
A superpowers drug
you can just rub into your skin?

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:48.789
You'd think it'd be something
you have to freebase.

00:04:48.872 --> 00:04:51.124
Let's see, which powers do we have?

00:04:51.208 --> 00:04:52.417
"Super strength"?

00:04:52.501 --> 00:04:53.752
Ah!

00:04:53.836 --> 00:04:55.420
Hi-ya!

00:04:55.504 --> 00:04:56.713
- Yup.
- Uh-huh.

00:04:56.797 --> 00:04:57.965
"Lickety-speed"?

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:00.717
- Check.
- Yes, sir.

00:05:01.593 --> 00:05:04.471
"Ability to command
the loyalty of sea creatures"?

00:05:04.555 --> 00:05:06.557
Hey, Zoidberg, get in here.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:08.225
Screw you!

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:09.434
- Ain't got that.
- Nope.

00:05:09.518 --> 00:05:11.311
Wow, superpowers.

00:05:11.395 --> 00:05:15.107
I'll be able to pack my day
with twice as many humdrum activities.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:17.651
Leela, I think you're missing
the big picture.

00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:20.153
When you were a kid,
what was your biggest fantasy?

00:05:20.237 --> 00:05:21.697
To have parents.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:24.783
Whatever.
The correct answer is to be a superhero.

00:05:24.867 --> 00:05:27.870
We have superpowers, and we're Americans.

00:05:27.953 --> 00:05:29.288
This is our chance.

00:05:29.371 --> 00:05:30.622
Hmm.

00:05:30.706 --> 00:05:33.166
I have been looking for
a way to serve the community

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:35.377
that incorporates my violence.

00:05:35.544 --> 00:05:36.712
Let's do it.

00:05:36.795 --> 00:05:38.338
You'll barely regret this.

00:05:38.881 --> 00:05:41.258
Hey, a friend of mine said
he mugged you today

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:42.718
and you had superpowers.

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:45.470
It's true, thanks
to this funky-fresh cream.

00:05:45.554 --> 00:05:48.682
Now me and Leela are forming
an awesome crime-fighting duo.

00:05:48.765 --> 00:05:51.226
Wow, crime fighting. Cool.

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:52.769
And you say you're a duo?

00:05:53.312 --> 00:05:54.855
Yeah, duos are good.

00:05:54.938 --> 00:05:57.191
Of course, sometimes
they're a little shorthanded.

00:05:58.317 --> 00:05:59.610
See, ya.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:04.239
With two humans, you'd think there'd be
a robot in there to balance things out.

00:06:04.823 --> 00:06:06.325
But whatever.

00:06:09.161 --> 00:06:11.788
I have these three costumes you could use,

00:06:11.872 --> 00:06:14.458
but I guess I'll just throw one away.

00:06:14.541 --> 00:06:16.418
We'd love to have you on the team, Bender,

00:06:16.502 --> 00:06:19.171
but aren't you more on
the supply side of crime?

00:06:19.254 --> 00:06:21.381
Plus, the cream
won't give you superpowers.

00:06:21.465 --> 00:06:22.549
You're a robot.

00:06:22.633 --> 00:06:25.010
So? I'm already super strong.

00:06:25.093 --> 00:06:26.428
And my arms do this.

00:06:32.684 --> 00:06:34.686
Also, I got this going.

00:06:41.818 --> 00:06:43.737
Listen up, New New York!

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:46.490
There's a new group of superheroes in town

00:06:46.573 --> 00:06:47.574
and we're...

00:06:47.658 --> 00:06:49.952
Quiet! It's 4:00 a.m.
and I just fell asleep

00:06:50.035 --> 00:06:52.204
for the first time in 30 years!

00:06:52.287 --> 00:06:53.789
Sorry!

00:06:53.872 --> 00:06:56.959
A new era of justice has begun.

00:06:57.042 --> 00:06:58.168
What?

00:07:01.713 --> 00:07:05.008
Attention,
all crooks,lowlifes and lawbreakers.

00:07:05.092 --> 00:07:08.428
Do yourselves a favor
and crawlback into your filthy tenements,

00:07:08.512 --> 00:07:10.055
you human cockroaches,

00:07:10.138 --> 00:07:13.851
or get your ugly face punched
to custard by...

00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:15.769
The New Justice Team!

00:07:15.853 --> 00:07:17.604
Captain Yesterday!

00:07:17.688 --> 00:07:19.147
Clobberella!

00:07:20.607 --> 00:07:23.986
And Super King, the best one of the three!

00:07:24.069 --> 00:07:25.070
Wow!

00:07:28.407 --> 00:07:30.450
Go, go, go, New Justice Team

00:07:30.534 --> 00:07:32.703
Go, team, go, team, team, team, team

00:07:32.786 --> 00:07:34.496
Who's the newest justice team?

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.748
The New Justice Team

00:07:36.832 --> 00:07:38.834
Captain Yesterday is fast

00:07:38.917 --> 00:07:40.836
Also he is from the past

00:07:40.919 --> 00:07:43.839
Not just fast but from the past

00:07:43.922 --> 00:07:45.883
Captain Yesterday

00:07:45.966 --> 00:07:47.676
Super King has all the powers

00:07:47.759 --> 00:07:49.803
Of a king plus all the powers

00:07:49.887 --> 00:07:52.472
Of Superman, also he's a robot

00:07:52.556 --> 00:07:54.474
Ain't it cool? Super King, you rule

00:07:56.768 --> 00:07:58.979
Clobberella beats you up

00:07:59.062 --> 00:08:01.315
Clobberella beats you up

00:08:01.398 --> 00:08:03.400
Who does she beat up? You!

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:05.110
Clobberella!

00:08:07.946 --> 00:08:10.073
Citizens, never fear

00:08:10.157 --> 00:08:12.326
Crazy do-good freaks are here

00:08:12.409 --> 00:08:15.287
Until they run out of steam

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:17.581
Miracle Cream, Miracle Cream

00:08:17.664 --> 00:08:19.917
Gives the power to the team

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.211
Its effects wear off for sure

00:08:22.294 --> 00:08:24.963
So they just slop on some more

00:08:26.507 --> 00:08:28.300
The New Justice Team!

00:08:28.884 --> 00:08:30.093
Ta-da!

00:08:33.138 --> 00:08:36.683
Captain Yesterday,
I find your skintight high-waters

00:08:36.767 --> 00:08:38.101
incredibly sexy.

00:08:38.185 --> 00:08:39.561
Let's get together sometime.

00:08:39.645 --> 00:08:41.355
Sure. I'm listed in the phone book.

00:08:41.438 --> 00:08:44.316
So once I reveal my real name to you,
along with my home address

00:08:44.399 --> 00:08:46.276
and a copy of my birth certificate...

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:47.778
Are you crazy?

00:08:47.861 --> 00:08:50.405
We have to keep
our secret identities secret.

00:08:50.489 --> 00:08:51.532
From everybody?

00:08:51.615 --> 00:08:53.575
Especially from everybody.

00:08:53.659 --> 00:08:55.160
Give several reasons why.

00:08:55.244 --> 00:08:58.830
For one, superheroes cause a lot
of collateral damage

00:08:58.914 --> 00:09:00.749
and we don't want to get our butts sued.

00:09:00.832 --> 00:09:02.251
Or do we?

00:09:02.918 --> 00:09:04.586
No, I guess not.

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:09.049
Also, if our identities get out,
every crook in the city will be after us

00:09:09.132 --> 00:09:11.301
or, God forbid, our loved ones.

00:09:11.385 --> 00:09:14.680
Super King has no need for loved ones.

00:09:16.265 --> 00:09:17.474
How you doing, kid?

00:09:20.769 --> 00:09:21.937
There you go.

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:24.147
Two one-day mutant surface passes.

00:09:24.231 --> 00:09:25.816
Thank you, Mayor Poopenmeyer.

00:09:27.276 --> 00:09:29.069
Mayor here. What's that?

00:09:29.152 --> 00:09:32.364
A horrible crime in the works?
Ruthless villain?

00:09:32.447 --> 00:09:34.032
Citizens in danger?

00:09:34.116 --> 00:09:36.285
That's fantastic news!

00:09:36.368 --> 00:09:39.788
Because I get to summon
The New Justice Team!

00:09:41.039 --> 00:09:42.082
Oh!

00:09:42.165 --> 00:09:43.458
Shh.

00:09:43.542 --> 00:09:45.460
Huh... They're usually here by now.

00:09:45.544 --> 00:09:47.838
Well, so long. Keep in touch.

00:09:47.921 --> 00:09:49.923
Wait, stay and meet the superheroes.

00:09:50.007 --> 00:09:52.426
There's three of you and three of them,
so it'll be perfect.

00:09:57.514 --> 00:09:58.807
Is this clown on?

00:09:58.891 --> 00:10:01.310
Where are those daring crime-stoppers?

00:10:01.393 --> 00:10:03.520
Oh, I completely forgot!

00:10:03.604 --> 00:10:06.106
I left my apartment on fire.

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:10.110
As for me, I'm late for my LSATs.

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:13.572
And I can't take life anymore!

00:10:18.535 --> 00:10:21.788
Clobberella! Captain Yesterday! My liege!

00:10:21.872 --> 00:10:23.665
You're just in time.

00:10:24.499 --> 00:10:27.711
We've received a tip
that the Museum of Natural History

00:10:27.794 --> 00:10:30.339
will be robbed tomorrow
at exactly 9:00 a.m.

00:10:30.839 --> 00:10:33.842
The target...
The priceless Quantum Gemerald.

00:10:33.926 --> 00:10:34.927
Who's the perp?

00:10:35.761 --> 00:10:38.305
A dangerous villain
known as the Zookeeper,

00:10:38.388 --> 00:10:41.683
who commits crimes
aided by a pack of highly trained animals.

00:10:41.767 --> 00:10:43.685
Pack of highly. Got it.

00:10:43.769 --> 00:10:46.146
His crew includes a badger
with a troubled past

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:47.523
and nothing left to lose,

00:10:47.606 --> 00:10:49.858
an elephant who never forgets to kill,

00:10:49.942 --> 00:10:56.073
and a seldom-used crab
named Lucky, aka "Citizen Snips."

00:10:57.991 --> 00:11:01.495
You can count on us, Mr. Mayor.
Justice away!

00:11:03.872 --> 00:11:06.375
Hold the elevator!

00:11:17.135 --> 00:11:18.262
We're in here, too.

00:11:18.345 --> 00:11:21.056
Uh, Leela, how are you
going to meet your folks tomorrow?

00:11:21.139 --> 00:11:24.810
We've already scheduled the Zookeeper
for a 9:00 a.m. foiling at the museum.

00:11:24.893 --> 00:11:25.936
Not a problem.

00:11:26.019 --> 00:11:28.689
I've cleverly arranged
to meet my parents right there

00:11:28.772 --> 00:11:30.524
at the same museum at 10:00.

00:11:30.816 --> 00:11:34.361
Nine, 10, a big fat hen.

00:11:35.112 --> 00:11:37.364
The name's Bender.

00:11:52.171 --> 00:11:55.757
I can't believe the Zookeeper
is this late for his own heist.

00:11:55.841 --> 00:11:57.509
It's just rude.

00:11:59.178 --> 00:12:01.263
Total hell! It's 10:00!

00:12:01.346 --> 00:12:04.683
I'm supposed to meet my parents
and I'm still in my secret costume.

00:12:06.185 --> 00:12:07.603
There they are!

00:12:10.047 --> 00:12:12.007
How could Leela not be here?

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:13.342
Do you think she forgot?

00:12:13.425 --> 00:12:16.094
Relax. I'm sure she's just ashamed of us.

00:12:16.178 --> 00:12:17.262
Yo, freakjobs.

00:12:17.346 --> 00:12:19.556
Hit the nearest manhole, pronto-like.

00:12:19.639 --> 00:12:22.184
But we have passes
that allow us to be up here,

00:12:22.267 --> 00:12:23.643
from the mayor himself.

00:12:25.312 --> 00:12:28.523
I don't know. I never heard of no mayor.

00:12:31.109 --> 00:12:32.361
The Zookeeper!

00:12:33.403 --> 00:12:35.530
Sorry I'm late. Long story.

00:12:35.864 --> 00:12:37.616
Now, everybody hit the deck!

00:12:37.699 --> 00:12:40.369
I'm cutting the entire line
and stealing the exhibit.

00:12:41.453 --> 00:12:44.122
You're not stealing anything.
Nobody hit the deck!

00:12:44.206 --> 00:12:46.500
Ah, the superheroes...

00:12:46.583 --> 00:12:48.794
Or should I say, "super zeroes?"

00:12:48.877 --> 00:12:50.337
That was uncalled for.

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:51.880
Animals, attack.

00:13:06.311 --> 00:13:08.772
Please do not feed the animals.

00:13:21.243 --> 00:13:23.328
You're going down, my friend!

00:13:23.412 --> 00:13:24.454
Down under!

00:13:28.667 --> 00:13:31.837
A man boxing a kangaroo
is a peculiar spectacle,

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:34.256
but a kangaroo boxing a robot?

00:13:34.339 --> 00:13:36.258
Now I'm afraid you've lost me.

00:13:37.884 --> 00:13:40.178
Citizen Snips!

00:13:47.394 --> 00:13:49.521
Nice job, Fingers.

00:13:51.273 --> 00:13:53.191
I'm scared and confused.

00:13:53.275 --> 00:13:56.403
I think we've wandered into
an off-Broadway play.

00:13:56.486 --> 00:13:58.196
No, there are way too many people here.

00:14:00.991 --> 00:14:04.703
Later, if anyone asks
when I got away, tell them right now.

00:14:06.863 --> 00:14:08.115
Forget it, Zookeeper.

00:14:08.198 --> 00:14:09.950
You're going into captivity.

00:14:10.033 --> 00:14:11.034
Fool!

00:14:11.159 --> 00:14:15.497
A quip about putting me behind bars
would have been far more delicious.

00:14:16.206 --> 00:14:17.666
Here, catch.

00:14:17.749 --> 00:14:20.377
No, Fry, you can't fall fast enough!

00:14:24.214 --> 00:14:25.590
I got it, I got it.

00:14:25.674 --> 00:14:26.967
I don't got it!

00:14:30.554 --> 00:14:32.139
You saved the Gemerald!

00:14:32.222 --> 00:14:34.266
Yet the Zookeeper escaped,

00:14:34.349 --> 00:14:38.979
thus proving that the deadliest
animal of all is the Zookeeper.

00:14:39.062 --> 00:14:40.564
You can get off me anytime.

00:14:40.647 --> 00:14:41.940
Oh, no.

00:14:42.024 --> 00:14:43.442
My parents are leaving.

00:14:43.525 --> 00:14:45.485
I've got to go change back
into street Leela.

00:14:45.569 --> 00:14:47.654
There they are.

00:14:47.738 --> 00:14:49.072
Thank you, mysterious heroes.

00:14:49.156 --> 00:14:51.867
The value of the Gemerald
you saved is slightly greater

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.870
than the cost of the damage
you caused to this museum.

00:14:54.953 --> 00:14:57.080
A net gain for our great city.

00:15:03.587 --> 00:15:05.839
It's good that Leela doesn't love us.

00:15:05.922 --> 00:15:07.966
She'll be less sad when we die.

00:15:17.809 --> 00:15:20.020
Mom, Dad?

00:15:20.103 --> 00:15:21.229
I showed up,

00:15:21.313 --> 00:15:24.566
and I got the audio tour
for "Treasures of Liberace's Tomb."

00:15:41.792 --> 00:15:43.502
Sweetie, it's okay.

00:15:43.585 --> 00:15:45.671
You don't have
to apologize for standing us up

00:15:45.754 --> 00:15:48.382
on the only visit
to the surface we'll ever have.

00:15:48.465 --> 00:15:51.635
I want to tell you why
I didn't show up, but I can't.

00:15:51.718 --> 00:15:55.263
Just please believe me
that it was a very good reason.

00:15:55.347 --> 00:15:57.516
I'm sorry I disappointed you.

00:15:59.268 --> 00:16:02.062
Leela, you could never disappoint us.

00:16:02.145 --> 00:16:04.815
We're so proud of everything that you are.

00:16:04.898 --> 00:16:06.733
And we always will be.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:09.027
Because you're our baby girl.

00:16:12.114 --> 00:16:13.156
Oh...

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:14.366
I can't take it.

00:16:14.449 --> 00:16:16.159
Mom, Dad...

00:16:16.243 --> 00:16:18.287
I'm Clobberella!

00:16:21.164 --> 00:16:22.916
Galloping gators!

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:24.710
You're a superhero?

00:16:24.793 --> 00:16:27.045
Well, that's wonderful.

00:16:27.129 --> 00:16:30.299
But did you have to make
the costume so revealing?

00:16:30.382 --> 00:16:34.177
Look at me, proud dad of a superhero.

00:16:34.261 --> 00:16:35.929
We should print up T-shirts.

00:16:36.013 --> 00:16:39.391
And F-shirts for our friends
with two arms on the same side.

00:16:39.474 --> 00:16:43.979
No, listen. It's very important
that you never ever tell anyone.

00:16:44.062 --> 00:16:45.731
Under any circumstance.

00:16:45.814 --> 00:16:47.107
What if I've had a few?

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:49.234
Dad? You drink?

00:16:49.318 --> 00:16:50.902
No, not even then.

00:16:50.986 --> 00:16:53.238
All right. My sucker is sealed.

00:16:53.739 --> 00:16:56.700
In fact, I shouldn't even
be wearing this around here.

00:16:58.535 --> 00:16:59.536
It was brisk.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:00.954
I dressed in layers.

00:17:01.038 --> 00:17:02.414
That's my girl.

00:17:08.295 --> 00:17:11.131
So, uh, anyway, my daughter's Clobberella.

00:17:11.214 --> 00:17:13.342
Leela is Clobberella?

00:17:13.425 --> 00:17:14.635
You're pulling me.

00:17:14.718 --> 00:17:16.136
Shh! Keep it under your sock.

00:17:16.219 --> 00:17:17.346
It's a big secret.

00:17:17.429 --> 00:17:18.889
That's why I'm only telling you two.

00:17:18.972 --> 00:17:21.600
Oh, my God.
That guy's daughter is Clobberella.

00:17:21.683 --> 00:17:23.101
But don't tell anyone.

00:17:23.185 --> 00:17:24.519
Gotcha!

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:30.275
Greeting, superheroes.

00:17:30.359 --> 00:17:31.652
Remember me?

00:17:31.735 --> 00:17:33.946
I don't remember much, buddy,

00:17:34.029 --> 00:17:35.614
and you're no looker.

00:17:35.697 --> 00:17:38.283
Uh, Professor, isn't it time for your nap?

00:17:38.367 --> 00:17:39.576
Yes, damn it!

00:17:45.374 --> 00:17:48.043
Zookeeper, how did you know
our real identities?

00:17:48.126 --> 00:17:51.630
Let's just say a little bird told me.

00:17:52.965 --> 00:17:54.216
Leela told her parents.

00:17:54.299 --> 00:17:56.593
Leela's parents blabbed...

00:17:58.095 --> 00:18:00.472
Leela? Is the person
that parrot is mimicking

00:18:00.555 --> 00:18:02.015
telling the truth by proxy?

00:18:02.432 --> 00:18:03.433
Yes.

00:18:03.517 --> 00:18:06.603
My parents were so hurt,
I couldn't help it.

00:18:06.687 --> 00:18:09.523
But I distinctly told them
not to tell anyone.

00:18:10.857 --> 00:18:12.901
We are not amused.

00:18:13.652 --> 00:18:16.863
And here's something you may
or may not find interesting.

00:18:19.866 --> 00:18:22.119
Mom! Dad!

00:18:22.202 --> 00:18:24.621
Leela, please forgive us.

00:18:24.705 --> 00:18:27.249
Especially your father,
who's the one who told!

00:18:27.332 --> 00:18:28.875
Thank you very much, Morris.

00:18:28.959 --> 00:18:30.836
Are you all right? Has he hurt you?

00:18:30.919 --> 00:18:33.422
No, but my allergies are going nuts.

00:18:34.756 --> 00:18:35.966
Oh, God!

00:18:36.049 --> 00:18:39.344
Every couch and table
has animal fur all over it.

00:18:39.428 --> 00:18:41.221
He lets them climb on everything.

00:18:41.305 --> 00:18:43.724
All right, Zookeeper, what do you want?

00:18:43.807 --> 00:18:46.226
Why, the Quantum Gemerald, of course.

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:48.270
You must steal it for me by midnight

00:18:48.353 --> 00:18:51.148
or your parents will be devoured
by piranhas that I have,

00:18:51.231 --> 00:18:55.277
shall we say,
persuaded to walk on dry land.

00:18:56.737 --> 00:18:57.946
Save us, Leela!

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:01.491
I mean, if you don't have
anything better to do.

00:19:04.202 --> 00:19:05.370
We're out of options.

00:19:05.454 --> 00:19:07.039
We have to steal the Gemerald.

00:19:07.164 --> 00:19:10.959
But should superheroes commit a crime,
even to save lives?

00:19:11.043 --> 00:19:12.419
I need moral guidance.

00:19:12.502 --> 00:19:13.920
- Bender?
- Hmm...

00:19:14.004 --> 00:19:17.716
The thought of stealing anything
fills Super King with disgust.

00:19:18.258 --> 00:19:22.763
But if it must be so,
than let a museum heist be pulled!

00:19:28.477 --> 00:19:31.396
Oh, no. Our superpower cream
is out of itself.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:32.564
Check inside the cap.

00:19:32.648 --> 00:19:34.650
There might be a caked-in gold mine.

00:19:36.693 --> 00:19:37.694
El zilcho.

00:19:37.778 --> 00:19:39.154
I'm afraid we're boned.

00:19:39.237 --> 00:19:40.530
El Zilcho...

00:19:40.614 --> 00:19:43.617
Hey, is it too late
to change my superhero name?

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:49.665
Just be cool.

00:19:49.748 --> 00:19:52.125
Nobody knows
we're superpowerly challenged.

00:19:53.502 --> 00:19:56.088
Man, this costume is so damn heavy.

00:19:56.171 --> 00:19:57.422
Hey, Captain Yesterday.

00:19:57.506 --> 00:20:00.717
Can I, like, whale on you with
this two-by-four and it doesn't hurt you?

00:20:00.801 --> 00:20:02.052
Ow!

00:20:02.135 --> 00:20:03.470
That didn't hurt.

00:20:04.388 --> 00:20:06.556
Hi, superheroes. Everything okay?

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:08.558
Big "O", little "K," my friend.

00:20:08.642 --> 00:20:10.269
Just checking if everything's all right.

00:20:10.352 --> 00:20:11.687
It's okay, all right.

00:20:11.770 --> 00:20:13.188
Okay, then.

00:20:13.897 --> 00:20:14.898
Grab it!

00:20:17.359 --> 00:20:21.029
Yo, the superheroes have turned evil.
Most uncool.

00:20:21.113 --> 00:20:22.114
Get 'em!

00:20:22.531 --> 00:20:23.740
Stay back!

00:20:23.824 --> 00:20:27.452
Or we'll beat the tar out of you,
using superpowers!

00:20:37.754 --> 00:20:39.464
So, this is your lair?

00:20:39.548 --> 00:20:40.757
Of course not.

00:20:40.841 --> 00:20:42.634
You think I'd show you my lair?

00:20:42.718 --> 00:20:44.970
My lair's a million times nicer than this.

00:20:45.053 --> 00:20:46.388
Okay, take it easy.

00:20:47.139 --> 00:20:49.308
Well, here's your lousy Gemerald.

00:20:49.391 --> 00:20:51.351
Hawk, fetch.

00:20:54.396 --> 00:20:55.897
That seemed unnecessary.

00:20:58.483 --> 00:21:00.485
Our transaction is complete.

00:21:00.569 --> 00:21:02.779
Come, Solomon, to the lair.

00:21:04.448 --> 00:21:05.699
Mom, Dad.

00:21:05.782 --> 00:21:08.994
Oh, I'm so sorry I got you
kidnapped by a crazy madman

00:21:09.077 --> 00:21:10.787
who tried to feed you to piranhas.

00:21:10.871 --> 00:21:13.915
We're just happy to be involved
in your life.

00:21:13.999 --> 00:21:17.878
No, no. It's my fault
for telling you I was a superhero.

00:21:17.961 --> 00:21:19.921
- That's true.
- I just couldn't stand

00:21:20.005 --> 00:21:21.923
to have you think I was ashamed of you.

00:21:22.007 --> 00:21:23.467
That's sweet, honey.

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:27.638
But it's natural for children
to be a little ashamed of their parents.

00:21:27.721 --> 00:21:29.681
- Oh, yeah.
- Just like it's natural

00:21:29.765 --> 00:21:32.267
for parents to be a little disappointed
in their children.

00:21:32.351 --> 00:21:33.685
Not that we are.

00:21:33.769 --> 00:21:36.313
But you could call a little more often.

00:21:36.396 --> 00:21:37.481
Okay.

00:21:37.564 --> 00:21:39.816
And would it kill you
to use some mouthwash?

00:21:42.194 --> 00:21:44.237
Hey, Fry, we still got our costumes on.

00:21:44.321 --> 00:21:45.864
Want to steal some more stuff?

00:21:45.948 --> 00:21:46.990
I guess.

00:21:47.074 --> 00:21:48.450
As long as you think it's right.

00:21:48.533 --> 00:21:52.204
Superheroes away!

00:22:01.838 --> 00:22:03.674
Go, go, go, New Justice Team

00:22:03.757 --> 00:22:05.926
Fighting justice is their quest

00:22:06.009 --> 00:22:09.846
Super King, Clobberella and all the rest

00:22:09.930 --> 00:22:12.391
Here's to you, New Justice Team

00:22:12.474 --> 00:22:14.559
Do the things that make a team

00:22:14.643 --> 00:22:16.895
Help each other do some things

00:22:16.979 --> 00:22:18.480
Winners don't use straws

00:22:23.902 --> 00:22:26.154
The New Justice Team!